---
import InnerPage from '../../layouts/InnerPage.astro';
import { BOOK_CALL_URL } from '../../config/site';
---

<InnerPage
	title="Career Navigator"
	description="How TeleTrex built a Career Navigator that turns an OntologyOfValue assessment and a résumé into a personalized job-match report — complete with target companies, roles, and ready-to-send outreach drafts."
>
	<p class="study__meta study__meta--top">Case Study · Custom AI workflow</p>
	<h1>Career Navigator: from assessment to first conversation</h1>
	<p class="page-lead">
		A career-coaching client wanted to turn raw psychometric data into action. We built Career
		Navigator — a tool that reads a candidate's OntologyOfValue assessment and résumé, asks a few
		targeted questions, and produces a personalized Career Navigator page plus a polished document
		pointing to the companies, roles, and people worth pursuing next.
	</p>

	<article class="study">
		<h2 class="study__title">The challenge</h2>
		<p class="prose-block">
			Candidates finishing the <a href="https://ontologyofvalue.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OntologyOfValue.com</a>
			assessment received a rich profile of their values, strengths, and motivations — but were
			often left asking "so what do I do with this?" The gap between self-knowledge and a concrete
			job search was wide: which companies fit my values, which roles match my experience, and how
			do I actually reach the right people without sounding generic?
		</p>
		<p class="prose-block">
			Coaches were bridging that gap by hand — reading results, cross-referencing résumés, and
			drafting outreach one candidate at a time. It was thoughtful work, but it didn't scale.
		</p>
	</article>

	<article class="study">
		<h2 class="study__title">What we built</h2>
		<p class="prose-block">
			Career Navigator ingests three inputs and turns them into a guided plan:
		</p>
		<ul class="prose-block study__list">
			<li>
				<strong>The OntologyOfValue assessment.</strong> The candidate's values and motivation
				profile becomes the lens for every recommendation — so matches reflect what they care
				about, not just what they've done.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>The résumé.</strong> We parse experience, skills, and trajectory to anchor
				recommendations in real, demonstrable qualifications.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>A short set of questions.</strong> A few targeted prompts about the work
				environment they want — team size, pace, remote vs. in-person, mission, compensation
				priorities — sharpen the search before any matching happens.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="prose-block">
			From there, the system generates a personalized <strong>Career Navigator page</strong> and a
			downloadable <strong>document</strong> that includes:
		</p>
		<ul class="prose-block study__list">
			<li><strong>Best-match companies</strong> — ranked against the candidate's values and the environment they described.</li>
			<li><strong>Best-fit positions</strong> — specific roles where their experience and motivations line up.</li>
			<li><strong>People to approach</strong> — relevant contacts at each target company.</li>
			<li><strong>Ready-to-send outreach</strong> — tailored sample drafts for email and LinkedIn, written in the candidate's voice and referencing why the fit is real.</li>
		</ul>
	</article>

	<article class="study">
		<h2 class="study__title">How it works</h2>
		<p class="prose-block">
			Career Navigator follows a simple flow that feels like a conversation with a coach rather than a
			form to fill out:
		</p>
		<ol class="prose-block study__list">
			<li><strong>Connect the data.</strong> The candidate brings their OntologyOfValue results and uploads their résumé.</li>
			<li><strong>Answer a few questions.</strong> The tool asks about the work environment they're looking for to focus the search.</li>
			<li><strong>Generate the navigator.</strong> The system synthesizes everything into a ranked, explained set of companies and roles.</li>
			<li><strong>Reach out.</strong> For each opportunity, it surfaces the right contacts and drafts personalized outreach the candidate can send with one edit.</li>
		</ol>
	</article>

	<article class="study">
		<h2 class="study__title">The result</h2>
		<p class="prose-block">
			Candidates leave the assessment with momentum instead of a question mark. Instead of a generic
			"good luck out there," they get a concrete, values-aligned target list and the words to start
			the conversation. Coaches scale their impact — the careful, personalized work they used to do
			by hand now happens in minutes, leaving them free to focus on the human coaching that software
			can't replace.
		</p>
		<p class="study__result"><strong>Result:</strong> Self-knowledge turned into a focused job search and warm outreach — assessment to first conversation, in one guided session.</p>
	</article>

	<p class="study cta-line">
		Want a tool like this for your own assessment or coaching practice?
		<a class="btn btn--primary" href={BOOK_CALL_URL}>Book a call</a>
	</p>
</InnerPage>

